Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Backport patch from SageMath

not sure whether it's still neded on macOS but it doesn't hurt.

Original commit:

commit 21464333b254d31bfe95801d575b203d9a9731cf
Author: Dima Pasechnik <dimpase@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Apr 12 10:14:53 2018 +0100

    Fixes miscompilation by clang from XCode 6.3, see #25118

    Without this, on most archs one gets "Illegal Instruction 4" error,
    probably due to an over-optimisation.
    As this is at the end of the main function, it is safe to just delete this delete.
---
 src/app_main.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/app_main.cpp b/src/app_main.cpp
index a33c042..dd34926 100644
--- a/src/app_main.cpp
+++ b/src/app_main.cpp
@@ -205,7 +205,6 @@ public:
     }
 
     ep->close();
-    delete ep;//<--- In next release, make the class virtual
 
     printf("\n");
 
